      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-183401",
      ":question/problem": "Use mathematical induction to prove that $n^{2} + n > 2n - 1$ for $n \u2208 N$.\n\nWe proceed using induction on $n$.\n\n**Base Case**: We first prove that our statement is true for the base case $n =$ {{field-1}}.\n\nFor the left-hand side, we have\n$1^{2} - 1$ {{field-2}} {{field-3}}\nwhich is {{field-4}} the right-hand side. Thus, our statement is {{field-5}} for $n = 1$."
    },
